    >[x] Classify habits files in every reader and archive path =core-habit-readers $One small reviewed increment; worker and independent reviewer from different vendors under dispatch. Add named tests before implementation, prove they execute (not a zero-test filtered pass), and pass clearhead-core/scripts/gate.sh before landing. Read docs/habit-transition-review.md inventory, then exhaustively search all *.actions readers. Teach Core assembly, action/sidecar mutation, CLI discovery/archive/doctor/publication and nvim init.lua stem/picker/archive/autocmd paths the full suffix. Acceptance: habit_reader_conformance tests root/flat/directory forms, templates, terminal files, archive moves and unrelated supporting files; no duplicate charter, live template child or archived Action leakage. Add nvim tests and run its documented test gate. Commit the completed caller inventory/guard; coordinate nvim release in this same cycle.  NOTE 2026-11-05 (steward): Core e726274 makes any do_date with R: an action-parse-error (parser.rs, do_date arm), restoring 0.3.2's refusal so no write drops a rule. This increment replaces that guard: habits files read R: into the Habit, and R: in a plain .actions file becomes the lint linting.md specifies, without ever being dropped on write.  BRIEF 2026-11-05 (steward, before run chr1): the inventory is specifications/docs/habit-transition-review.md. Scope: classify and read <charter>.habits.actions into Core's native Habit (from =core-habit-graph) wherever *.actions files are found; Habits never appear as Actions in live views, and nothing generates occurrences yet (=core-habit-catchup). Replace the e726274 refusal: in a habits file R: is the Habit's rule (E002 for a bad or missing one); in a plain .actions file or a named template R: is the linting.md Habit scope warning and survives every write byte for byte (a test writes such a file through a CLI mutation and diffs it). No specification change; if the published spec does not answer a reade